Changes
-------

All changes were made in 2026 by kw495, starting from Audio Share v0.3.4
(commit 342751f). The full history is in the git log of this repository.

- Server: stop sending while the captured audio is silent (silence gate)
- Server: convert the captured audio itself (any PCM format, mono/stereo,
  resampling), because WASAPI loopback only delivers the device mix format
- Server: Opus compression (--encoding=opus, --opus-bitrate)
- Server: a synthesized Morse code test tone that needs no sound device;
  capture errors no longer terminate the Windows GUI
- Windows GUI: channel and quality settings, test tone, Japanese translation
- Protocol: AudioFormat.encoding ENCODING_OPUS and AudioFormat.bitrate
- Android: choice of output stream (media, alarm, notification, ringtone),
  Opus decoding, connection status/format/statistics/log on the home screen,
  Japanese translation
- Update checks and project links point to https://github.com/kw495/audio-share

